<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malatya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malatya is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. After the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>, it was the centre of one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-hittite-states">Neo-Hittite states</a> that preserved Hittite political and artistic traditions. Like other such states, it was eventually absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malatya.jpg" alt="Malatya" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: L.Versoa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turgut_%C3%96zal_Tabiat_Park%C4%B1_G%C3%B6l.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
